T: Trevor Hart gives Charlie Dabbs a 38 secs lead after three stages. RIGHT: Bill Kerr takes the baton from Gerry North to chase J. Cooke on Stage 9.","id":"B155-10","w":"February 1965"},{"f":"crops/B157/B157-p14-hart-walker-handover.jpg","c":"Trevor Hart hands over to Charlie Walker with Weatherill (Portsmouth) waiting to take over from the fast-finishing Tulloh.","id":"B157-28","w":"November 1965"},{"f":"crops/B157/B157-p23-sunday-morning-at-arthurs.jpg","c":"SUNDAY MORNING AT ARTHUR'S Some of the \"gang\" enjoying refreshments---and Ron Linstead's clowning---on the lawn of Lauriston Cottage. L. to R. (rear)Charlie Dabbs, Charlie Smart,Trevor Hart,Ron Mitchell,Arthur Bruce,Howard Satchell,Ron Linstead,Mel Thorpe,John Thresher. L. to R. (front)Peter Wrench,John Dear,Gordon Biscoe,Charlie Manning.","id":"B157-49","w":"November 1965"},{"f":"crops/B158/B158-p25-dance-with-team.jpg","c":"My picture shows Bill (far right) alongside Chris Steer, our President Bob Taylor, Trevor Hart and Alan Black; with the two Norths and Dabbs in the front row.","id":"B158-52","w":"March 1966"},{"f":"crops/B158/B158-p31-hart-and-dabbs.jpg","c":"TOP LEFT: Trevor Hart and Charlie Dabbs commence lap 2.","id":"B158-61","w":"March 1966"},{"f":"crops/B160/B160-p15-dabbs-to-hart.jpg","c":"Left; Charlie Dabbs gives Trevor Hart a 32 seconds lead","id":"B160-30","w":"December 1966"},{"f":"crops/B161/B161-p20-club-10-miles-hart-fairclough-kerr-walker.jpg","c":"LEFT: Hart leads Fairclough in the chase for O'Hara. RIGHT: Bill Kerr paces \"World Sports\" star Charlie Walker!","id":"B161-29","w":"March 1967"},{"f":"crops/B161/B161-p25-trevor-hart-southern.jpg","c":"Trevor Hart once again produced his usual stolid performance and, on the Parliament Hill course he loves, closed in our scoring six.","id":"B161-37","w":"March 1967"},{"f":"crops/B161/B161-p43-national-backpiece-montage.jpg","c":"BACKPIECE PHOTOS: TOP LEFT: Barefooted Hart in the throes of a 9 miles battle with Dai Davies (TVH) who pipped him by one place. TOP RIGHT: Bicourt leads Ward (Man.DLC), Billings (Sutt.in A) and team-mate O'Hara. John finished one place ahead of Billings and 23 up on Ward. BOTTOM: A desperate North fights to hold off Bob Holt, Peter Welsh (Empire S'chase gold-medallist) and Mike Turner.","id":"B161-66","w":"March 1967"},{"f":"crops/B162/B162-p01-trevor-hart-cover.jpg","c":"FRONT COVER (Photo:R. Linstead) Trevor Hart, Belgrave's leading distance runner this season with times of 1:46:19 (Finchley 20) and 1:47:07 (Inter-County 20)","id":"B162-01","w":"June 1967"},{"f":"crops/B170/B170-p02-hart-piotrowski-national-relay.jpg","c":"FRONTISPIECE: (Ron Linstead) BELGRAVE take \"Silver\" in the National Relay at Leicester, and here is Trevor Hart handing over to Dick Piotrowski at the end of stage 8, in third place and 47 seconds behind the ultimate winners, Coventry Godiva.","id":"B170-02","w":"June 1969"},{"f":"crops/B172/B172-p15-johnston-relay-winning-team.jpg","c":"THE WINNING \"JOHNSTONE\" TEAM (Photo:David Hart)\nBACK ROW(l.to.r.):G.Biscoe(Manager),A.Fairclough(Reserve),R.Piotrowski,L.O'Hara,P.Morris, P.O'Connor.\nFRONT ROW(l.to.r.):G.W.Dance,J.Thresher,Gerry North(Captain),Geoff North,T.Hart.\nNote:L. Mann is absent--under escort back to the Palace!.","id":"B172-30","w":"December 1969"},{"f":"crops/B173/B173-p37-ohara-hart-coulsdon.jpg","c":"O'HARA and HART, 3rd and 4th scorers at Coulsdon.","id":"B173-84","w":"March 1970"},{"f":"crops/B174/B174-p19-trevor-hart-poly-marathon.jpg","c":"Trevor Hart, leading here from J. Wight (Edinburgh S.) in the closing stages, a new Club marathon record of 2:25:58.","id":"B174-35","w":"June 1970"},{"f":"crops/B177/B177-p16-road-race-runners.jpg","c":"The 5¾-miles championship field, still hunched after one mile. Front row: Pat O'Connor (12), Tony Fairclough (21), Peter Carton (19), Trevor Hart (23), and Lionel Mann (9). The three framed heads look like those of Chris Steer, John Thresher and Dereck Fernee.","id":"B177-34","w":"June 1971"},{"f":"crops/B178/B178-p32-oconnor-hart-handover.jpg","c":"Pat O'Connor hands over to Trevor Hart at the end of stage 9. in 3rd place.","id":"B178-72","w":"September 1972"},{"f":"crops/B180/B180-p29-trevor-hart.jpg","c":"First right: Trevor Hart gives his Middlesex vest an airing.","id":"B180-48","w":"March 1973"},{"f":"crops/B182/B182-p39-belgrave-20-montage.jpg","c":"The Belgrave 20 Mile Road Race. Centre: Graham Taylor (Camb H), the winner. Top left to right: Geoff Pearson, George Piddington, Alan Black and Trevor Hart. Bottom: John Davies, Bob Richardson and Charlie Henn.","id":"B182-65","w":"September 1973"},{"f":"crops/B201/B201-p48-flanagan-hart-relay.jpg","c":"A trip down memory lane. George Flanagan hands over to Trevor Hart in the 100 x 1 mile relay.","id":"B201-93","w":"October 1980"},{"f":"crops/B230/B230-p27-lauriston-cottage-1963.jpg","c":"Outside Arthur Whitehead's cottage on a Sunday morning in 1963. Back row: Brian Nott, ?, ?, Arthur Penstone, Ken Miller, Charlie Smart. Front row: Bill Kerr, Ron Linstead, Trevor Hart.","id":"B230-45","w":"June 2003"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B153/B153-p31-brighton-relay-montage.jpg","caption":"TOP LEFT: Bill Kerr trails Bullivant and Tulloh on Stage 9. TOP RIGHT: John Thresher hands over to a determined Trevor Hart after stage 2. CENTRE: Alan Mead and 'Noddy' Edwards, with some female assistance, cheer on the runners! BOTTOM LEFT: Laurie O'Hara hands over to Gerry North after chopping 17 secs off the Club record for stage 7. BOTTOM RIGHT: Alan Black brings Belgrave home in 4th place.","source":"B153-54","when":"April 1964"},"slarchive":"https://slarchive.org/#athlete/trevor-hart","slRaces":21,"x":1,"share":{"d":"Trevor Hart in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1960–2006: 365 mentions in 69 issues, 253 race results and 22 photographs. Wrote or reported 1 item.","img":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/home/faces/p-trevor-hart.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/b